file @compileFor(!ARCH_WASM32);

// Kept on every NON-wasm build and gone entirely on a wasm one — the file, its `export`, its `import`
// and every declaration in it.
//
// ⚠️ The duplicate name is the PROOF, and it is why this fixture cannot pass on a gate that does
// nothing. `platformValue` is declared here AND in impl_wasm.kama, and kama has no overloading, so if
// both files were ever admitted to one build the compiler would reject it — measured, before this fixture
// was trusted: with the two gate lines deleted, both legs fail with "duplicate function 'platformValue'".
// An exit-code fixture over a gate that merely DEACTIVATED a file rather than excluding it would still
// have returned 41 and told us nothing.
export { platformValue };

fn int32 platformValue() { return 40; }
